hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2870","Narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and 'Ali ibn Khashram — they all said:\nNarrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of 'Amr, on the authority of 'Ata', who said:\nI heard Ibn 'Abbas (RA) say:\n\I am among those whom the Prophet (ﷺ) sent forward on the night of Muzdalifah from among the weak members of his family.\""\n\nAbu 'Ammar"","" al-Makhzumi"","" and 'Ali also narrated it from Ibn 'Abbas (RA).\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
"2871","Narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ, narrated to us ʿAbd al-Razzāq, informed us Maʿmar, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar (RA) that he used to send the weak among his family ahead of him. They would stand at al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām at night, supplicating to Allah as they wished, then depart. Some of them would reach Minā by the time of Fajr prayer, while others would arrive later. These were the weak among his family. And he (Ibn ʿUmar) would say, \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted permission for this.\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
